 large pion-induced gradient and weaken the bound on the original de Sitter conjecture?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0032"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:602ea4010f973bdd2b6dc782eb95531e6bd512d1b1ba0bfadab3a1e80759790d","title":"Can a throat with slowly running AdS-like asymptotics contain a stable supersymmetry-breaking infrared sector? The motivating application is redshifted vacuum energy for four-dimensional uplift.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0034"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:6081a1b036118c5b586f8cac8b8ff923f48f5408baa0fa576c17535d73d16ba7","title":"Can selected quintessence potentials explain late cosmic acceleration, have their shape parameters constrained by cosmological observations, relieve the H0 tension, and compete statistically with ΛCDM?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0034"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:603e025f78e9f821a61c97becfb35dc0f4d9a282942860b6bc69dc8dfd5d4acd","title":"Does a small quintessence vacuum energy automatically imply a sufficiently small slope after radiative corrections, or must the two quantities be adjusted independently? The target also includes consistency with fifth-force observations.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0036"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:60774f133d3beece5114dec5186a02a24fc038437d660e3afe472e458a028673","title":"Can Scherk–Schwarz compactifications of open string theory have exponentially suppressed or positive one-loop vacuum energy without developing tachyonic Wilson-line moduli?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0037"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:60fda2fa93af519b7964403dde9c27133d61f7e61f7b16d950765805ee641b09","title":"Are the nearly tensionless strings in four-dimensional Type IIA two-f